WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.934
-Welcome. Enjoy yourself.
Welcome, welcome, welcome to

00:00:02.934 --> 00:00:04.133
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:05.501
You're here.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:05.501 --> 00:00:08.868
[ Cheering and applause ]
Yeah!

00:00:08.868 --> 00:00:10.200
Well, guys, this weekend is

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:13.033
the annual White House
Correspondents' Dinner.

00:00:13.033 --> 00:00:15.234
It's the black tie event
attended by the president,

00:00:15.234 --> 00:00:17.067
celebrities, and journalists,

00:00:17.067 --> 00:00:18.534
and I'm hearing
that Tucker Carlson

00:00:18.534 --> 00:00:20.434
and Don Lemon are expected
to be there.

00:00:20.434 --> 00:00:21.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:21.701 --> 00:00:24.467
As waiters, but, still,
they're going to --

00:00:24.467 --> 00:00:26.067
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:00:26.067 --> 00:00:27.934
Yeah, President Biden
will get up and tell jokes.

00:00:27.934 --> 00:00:29.367
It's fun because it's
the one night a year

00:00:29.367 --> 00:00:30.801
Biden gets laughs on purpose.

00:00:30.801 --> 00:00:33.334
[ Laughter and applause ]
And, you know, at Biden's age,

00:00:33.334 --> 00:00:34.968
the hardest part
of doing stand-up is

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:35.767
the standing up.

00:00:35.767 --> 00:00:37.434
[ Laughter, oohs, and applause ]

00:00:37.434 --> 00:00:38.968
Presidents always tell jokes

00:00:38.968 --> 00:00:40.467
at the White House
Correspondents' Dinner,

00:00:40.467 --> 00:00:43.033
but we're not the only country
with that tradition.

00:00:43.033 --> 00:00:44.901
Yep, just last weekend,
Vladimir Putin appeared

00:00:44.901 --> 00:00:46.501
at the Kremlin
Correspondents' Dinner.

00:00:46.501 --> 00:00:48.400
[ Laughter ]
Here's how it went.

00:00:51.334 --> 00:00:52.033
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:57.267
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:58.100 --> 00:00:59.467
[ Feedback whines ]

00:01:00.534 --> 00:01:02.234
[ Laughter and applause ]
-There we go.

00:01:02.234 --> 00:01:05.000
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:06.067
"Oh, yeah."

00:01:06.067 --> 00:01:06.734
[Indistinct]

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:11.033
Well, last night,
former President Trump

00:01:11.033 --> 00:01:12.801
held a rally in New Hampshire,

00:01:12.801 --> 00:01:14.467
where he unveiled
his new nickname

00:01:14.467 --> 00:01:16.634
for President Biden.
-Oh.
-Mm.

00:01:16.634 --> 00:01:18.467
-Now, he's had over two years
to think about this.

00:01:18.467 --> 00:01:19.968
[ Laughter ]
Let's see what he came up with.

00:01:19.968 --> 00:01:22.868
-This is going to be
a major announcement.

00:01:22.868 --> 00:01:25.033
Are you ready?
I will be retiring

00:01:25.033 --> 00:01:28.267
the name Crooked
from Hillary Clinton.

00:01:28.267 --> 00:01:32.200
-[ Protesting ]
-I'm going to retire
the name Crooked,

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:35.300
so that we can use the name
for Joe Biden.

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:38.300
[ Cheering ]
He'll be known, from now on,
as Crooked Joe Biden.

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:41.267
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:43.400
-A little lazy.
I don't know.

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.067
Pretty lazy with the names.
I'm starting to understand

00:01:45.067 --> 00:01:46.667
how he came up with Don Jr.,
you know?

00:01:46.667 --> 00:01:48.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:48.701 --> 00:01:50.234
I was hoping for something
better than that.

00:01:50.234 --> 00:01:52.334
Even Biden was like,
"How'd you miss Sloppy Joe?

00:01:52.334 --> 00:01:54.667
[ Laughter and applause ]
Come on."

00:01:54.667 --> 00:01:56.434
Biden actually wants
to give Trump a nickname,

00:01:56.434 --> 00:01:58.267
but nothing's funnier
than one term.

00:01:58.267 --> 00:02:01.133
[ Laughter and ohhs ]
-Ah!

00:02:01.133 --> 00:02:03.367
[ Cheering and applause ]
Come on!
-Ooh!

00:02:03.367 --> 00:02:05.000
Ooh! Ooh!
-Yeah! Come on!

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:07.100
-Ooh!
Use that this weekend.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:08.400
Use that at the dinner, yeah.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:09.734
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.734 --> 00:02:11.334
Trump wasn't just coming up
with nicknames.

00:02:11.334 --> 00:02:12.567
He also said that he and Biden

00:02:12.567 --> 00:02:14.934
have some unfinished business
to settle.

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:17.234
[ Laughter and oohs ]
-Trump was like --

00:02:17.234 --> 00:02:18.601
[ As Trump ]
I know how to finish business.

00:02:18.601 --> 00:02:20.567
That's why all my businesses
are finished.

00:02:20.567 --> 00:02:23.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:23.734 --> 00:02:27.234
[ Cheering ]

00:02:27.234 --> 00:02:30.267
Get this -- despite Trump's
best efforts to block it,

00:02:30.267 --> 00:02:33.400
Mike Pence testified
for over five hours

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:36.601
in front of the grand jury
investigating January 6th.

00:02:36.601 --> 00:02:38.934
Wow, five hours
of Mike Pence testimony.

00:02:38.934 --> 00:02:40.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.167 --> 00:02:41.801
The grand jury was like,
"Hey, Trump did the crime.

00:02:41.801 --> 00:02:43.901
Why are we being punished?
I don't understand
what's happening."

00:02:43.901 --> 00:02:45.434
[ Laughter and applause ]
Just to keep everyone awake,

00:02:45.434 --> 00:02:47.834
they pumped oxygen into the room
like it was Caesars Palace.

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:49.634
There you go.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:49.634 --> 00:02:51.033
Some more political news --
next month,

00:02:51.033 --> 00:02:52.834
Republican Senator Tim Scott

00:02:52.834 --> 00:02:55.868
is expected to launch
his presidential campaign.

00:02:55.868 --> 00:02:56.868
The only thing is
a lot of people

00:02:56.868 --> 00:02:58.467
aren't familiar with Tim Scott

00:02:58.467 --> 00:03:00.501
or with other senators,
for that matter,

00:03:00.501 --> 00:03:02.701
so, I thought I'd help you out
really quick.

00:03:02.701 --> 00:03:06.868
♪♪

00:03:10.234 --> 00:03:10.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.934 --> 00:03:12.934
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.901 --> 00:03:14.868
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.968 --> 00:03:16.000
♪ This is Tim ♪

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.000
♪ This is Rick ♪

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:17.934
♪ This is Tim ♪

00:03:17.934 --> 00:03:18.901
♪ But isn't him ♪

00:03:18.901 --> 00:03:20.434
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.901 --> 00:03:24.834
♪ Two Tims ♪

00:03:24.834 --> 00:03:26.033
♪ Diff names ♪

00:03:26.033 --> 00:03:26.868
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.868 --> 00:03:28.968
♪ Tim, Rick, Tim, Tom ♪

00:03:28.968 --> 00:03:31.000
♪ Tom, Jim, Rick Scott ♪

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:32.968
♪ Jim, Tim, Tom's their name ♪

00:03:32.968 --> 00:03:34.968
♪ Also Thom, but with an H ♪

00:03:34.968 --> 00:03:37.000
[ Laughter ]
♪ Mark, Bob, Mark, Bob ♪

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:38.968
♪ Rick, Rick, Markwayne ♪

00:03:38.968 --> 00:03:40.968
[ Laughter ]
♪ Bob, Mark, Bob, Todd ♪

00:03:40.968 --> 00:03:42.934
♪ Ed Markey, back to Kaine ♪

00:03:42.934 --> 00:03:44.934
[ Laughter ]
♪ John and John
and John and John ♪

00:03:44.934 --> 00:03:46.968
♪ And John and John
and John, okay? ♪

00:03:46.968 --> 00:03:48.934
♪ Also Jon, also Jon ♪

00:03:48.934 --> 00:03:50.968
♪ But those last two
don't have an H ♪

00:03:50.968 --> 00:03:52.934
♪ Tim, Tom, Jim, Bob,
Markwayne, Rick Scott ♪

00:03:52.934 --> 00:03:53.934
♪ Tim, Tom, Jim Risch ♪

00:03:53.934 --> 00:03:55.067
♪ Rickroll, Tim Scott ♪

00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:58.334
[ Cheering and applause ]
[ Rimshot ]

00:03:59.701 --> 00:04:00.701
-Wow!

00:04:05.067 --> 00:04:08.601
-I hope that was helpful.

00:04:08.601 --> 00:04:12.200
I hope that was helpful.
-Oh, good, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:14.234
-Hey, listen to this --
today officials announced that,

00:04:14.234 --> 00:04:16.167
ahead of King Charles'
coronation,

00:04:16.167 --> 00:04:19.534
the historic stone called
the Stone of Scone

00:04:19.534 --> 00:04:22.434
[ Laughter ]
